msgid ""
"<p>This is normal because there are several types of mathoms.<br>This "
"setting only applies to file and local link mathoms.<br>The images you see "
"are image mathoms, not file mathoms.<br>File mathoms are generic documents, "
"whereas image mathoms are pictures you can draw in.</p><p>When dropping "
"files to locations, %1 detects their type and shows you the content of the "
"files.<br>For instance, when dropping image or text files, image and text "
"mathoms are created for them.<br>For type of files %2 does not understand, "
"they are shown as generic file mathoms with just an icon or file preview and "
"a filename.</p><p>If you do not want the application to create mathoms "
"depending on the content of the files you drop, go to the \"General\" page "
"and uncheck \"Image or animation\" in the \"View Content of Added Files for "
"the Following Types\" group.</p>"
